  "situation": "An F-16C mishap occurred in Clinton, Maryland, on 5 April 2017. The engine experienced overspeed, overtemperature, fire, and catastrophic failure. The MEC regulates fuel flow and variable stator vane position, and omission or improper installation of its small components can cause malfunction and possible aircraft loss. The differential-pressure pilot valve was found without a required retaining ring and anti-rotation pin. MEC work-control documents did not require parts inventory after disassembly or before assembly, and some kits and retained parts included excess components. Other considerations included the technician’s decision about reusing serviceable parts, the small size of the missing pin, task complexity, and human error; misassembly could still have occurred with an adequate accountability program.",
